This is a placeholder for the UMG Widget Blueprint file. 

In Unreal Engine Editor, you need to:

1. Create a new folder: Content/UI/
2. Right-click → User Interface → Widget Blueprint
3. Name it: WBP_PauseMenu

Widget Structure:
=================

Canvas Panel (Root)
├── Image (BackgroundBlur)
│   ├── Anchor: Fill Screen
│   ├── Tint: Black (R:0, G:0, B:0, A:0.7)
│   └── Brush: White Square
│
└── Vertical Box (MenuContainer) 
    ├── Anchor: Center
    ├── Alignment: 0.5, 0.5
    ├── Size: Auto
    │
    ├── Text Block (Title)
    │   ├── Text: "Menu Pause"
    │   ├── Font Size: 48
    │   ├── Color: White
    │   └── Justification: Center
    │
    ├── Spacer (Height: 30)
    │
    ├── Button (ResumeButton)
    │   ├── Size: 250x50
    │   └── Text Block (ResumeText): "Reprendre"
    │
    ├── Spacer (Height: 10)
    │
    ├── Button (OptionsButton)
    │   ├── Size: 250x50
    │   └── Text Block (OptionsText): "Options"
    │
    ├── Spacer (Height: 10)
    │
    ├── Button (RestartButton)
    │   ├── Size: 250x50
    │   └── Text Block (RestartText): "Recommencer"
    │
    ├── Spacer (Height: 10)
    │
    └── Button (QuitButton)
        ├── Size: 250x50
        └── Text Block (QuitText): "Quitter"

Button Events (In the Graph Editor):
===================================

For ResumeButton OnClicked:
- Get Player Controller → Cast to GameplayPlayerController → ResumeGame

For RestartButton OnClicked:
- Get Player Controller → Cast to GameplayPlayerController → RestartLevel

For QuitButton OnClicked:
- Get Player Controller → Cast to GameplayPlayerController → ReturnToMainMenu

For OptionsButton OnClicked:
- (To be implemented later - placeholder for options menu)

Blueprint Variables:
===================
None needed for basic functionality.

Animations (Optional):
=====================
- Create "FadeIn" animation for smooth appearance
- Animate the MenuContainer with a scale from 0.8 to 1.0 over 0.2 seconds